class.description:
A parked call is identified by an id rather than by its position, because [method sweep] moves rows and the thing that resolves a call is a closure written when it was parked. [method resolve] answers whether the call was still waiting, so a call that already ran or already timed out cannot run a second time.
The per-sender budget of 100 is what keeps a peer naming routes nobody has from growing the book without bound. A refused park is counted by [method refused], never queued, so the refusal is visible as a number rather than as a delay.
[codeblock]
var id := park.park(sender, route, tick + timeout)
if id < 0:
    return                       # this sender is at its budget
api.when_live(route, func():
    if park.resolve(id):
        run_the_call())
[/codeblock]
